id:                     DRAFT-9995
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         2404_87638649
trigger_tool:           cmake|clang|ctest|binary-sign-tool
phase:                  build|test
error_signature:        use of undeclared identifier 'glDispatchCompute'|
                         use of undeclared identifier 'GL_SHADER_STORAGE_BARRIER_BIT'|
                         use of undeclared identifier 'GL_TIME_ELAPSED'|
                         use of undeclared identifier 'glGetQueryObjectiv'; did you mean 'glGetQueryObjectuiv'|
                         Error loading shared library \.\./lib/libf3d\.so|
                         Error loading shared library libvtk[A-Za-z]+-9\.4\.so\.1.*Permission denied|
                         install TARGETS RUNTIME_DEPENDENCY_SET is not supported on system "HarmonyOS"

severity:               2
category:               gles|egl|vtk|codesign|soname|cmake|ohos-loader
match_keywords:         vtk_glad.h, GLES3/gl31.h, glDispatchCompute, glMemoryBarrier,
                         GL_TIME_ELAPSED, EXT_disjoint_timer_query, gl2ext.h,
                         GL_GLEXT_PROTOTYPES, codesign sidecar, binary-sign-tool,
                         selfSign, dlopen Permission denied, SONAME, DT_NEEDED,
                         ../lib/ relative path, ctest WORKING_DIRECTORY,
                         F3D_TESTING_FORCE_RENDERING_BACKEND, EGL offscreen

root_cause: |
  VTK 9.4.1 built with VTK_OPENGL_USE_GLES serves vtk_glad.h which in GLES3
  mode only includes <GLES3/gl3.h>. Consumers using GLES 3.1+ APIs
  (compute shaders: glDispatchCompute/glMemoryBarrier; timer queries:
  GL_TIME_ELAPSED/glGetQueryObjectiv) fail to compile because those are
  declared in gl31.h / the EXT_disjoint_timer_query block of gl2ext.h.
  Additionally, on OHOS two runtime blockers prevent ctest from running
  VTK-linked binaries: (a) libs without an explicit SONAME get the
  build-tree relative path ("../lib/libf3d.so") in consumers' DT_NEEDED,
  unresolvable from ctest's CMake-binary-dir CWD; (b) the OHOS loader
  requires a valid .codesign section for dlopen, and HMDFS keeps the
  signature as sidecar data which conan's copy into the package cache
  does not preserve ("Permission denied" on every dependency .so).

rec_approach: |
  1. GLES 3.1 compute APIs: after #include <vtk_glad.h> add
     #if defined(GL_ES_VERSION_3_0)
     #include <GLES3/gl31.h>
     #endif
  2. Timer query: #define GL_GLEXT_PROTOTYPES 1 + #include <GLES2/gl2ext.h>,
     then map GL_TIME_ELAPSED -> GL_TIME_ELAPSED_EXT and
     glGetQueryObjectiv -> glGetQueryObjectivEXT.
  3. Bare SONAMEs: set_target_properties(<lib> PROPERTIES LINK_FLAGS
     "-Wl,-soname,lib<name>.so") guarded by
     CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "HarmonyOS"; prepend the build lib dir to
     ctest's LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
  4. Re-sign dependency .so before running tests:
     binary-sign-tool sign -selfSign 1 -inFile <so> -outFile <so>.signed
     then os.replace() (tool available at /data/service/hnp/bin/).
  Verified on f3d 3.5.0 + VTK 9.4.1 (Maleoon 916, GLES 3.2): upstream
  suite goes from 0/1018 (not runnable) to 523/630 (83%) real passes.

fallback: |
  If binary-sign-tool is unavailable (non-OHOS hosts), skip the re-sign
  step and skip upstream test execution via an EGL/capability probe —
  record the skip reason in the build log (CI headless path).

verify_builds:         PR #9995 conan create 2026-09-18 (523/630 = 83% on device)

related_rules:          P017, P019
related_entries:        E207 (SONAME missing — same root cause for ./lib relative links), E077 (re-sign via binary-sign-tool post-install), E083 (selfSign JNI libs), E318 (compile-sign-run go tests)
